    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0419" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1622: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-03T16:00:00+09:00">August 3, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 3—7:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>660. Department’s 286, July 31, noon.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d439-f1"/> The sense
                    of the President’s informal comments on Mr. Matsuoka’s private message<anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d439-f2"/> was communicated informally to him today by me.
                    Mr. Matsuoka listened with interest and asked me to express to the President his
                    full appreciation <pb facs="0420" n="412" xml:id="pg412"/> of the President’s
                    kindness and the trouble he had taken in commenting on the message.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
